# The Lie algebra so(3), the algebra of rotations of space (and su(2), the spin algebra), modeled by its bracket and
# proved to satisfy the Lie axioms by the kernel. The three generators are the rotations about the three axes; their
# bracket is the cross product, [e1,e2] = e3 and cyclically, the structure constants being the fully antisymmetric symbol.
# A bracket of two generators is a signed generator or zero. The kernel proves the bracket is ALTERNATING ([a,a] = 0, a
# rotation does not curve against itself) and ANTISYMMETRIC ([a,b] = -[b,a], the defining skew-symmetry of a Lie algebra),
# by exhaustive induction over the three axes. This is the smallest nonabelian Lie algebra, the tangent structure of the
# rotation group whose double cover is the spin one-half of matter, and the same bracket shape every gauge force carries.

# The three axes of rotation.
form axis
  case a1
  case a2
  case a3

# A bracket value: zero, or a signed generator.
form turn
  case still
  case pos
    link axis, like axis
  case neg
    link axis, like axis

# Negate a bracket value.
task flip-turn
  take t, like turn
  like turn
  fork case, read t
    case still
      send back
        make still
    case pos
      link axis
      send back
        make neg
          bind axis
            read axis
    case neg
      link axis
      send back
        make pos
          bind axis
            read axis

# TEMPLATE: a diagonal entry of the bracket table, [a,a] = 0. Replaces each `case .. / send back / make still` block.
tree bracket-still
  take col

  hook fuse
    case {col}
      send back
        make still

# TEMPLATE: an off-diagonal entry of the bracket table, the signed generator [a,b] = (sign) e_ax. Replaces each
# `case .. / send back / make pos|neg / bind axis / make ..` block with one line per entry.
tree bracket-turn
  take col
  take sign
  take ax

  hook fuse
    case {col}
      send back
        make {sign}
          bind axis
            make {ax}

# The Lie bracket of two generators, the cross product: [e1,e2]=e3, [e2,e3]=e1, [e3,e1]=e2, antisymmetric, zero on the
# diagonal. The structure constants of so(3).
task bracket
  take a, like axis
  take b, like axis
  like turn
  fork case, read a
    case a1
      fork case, read b
        fuse bracket-still, a1
        fuse bracket-turn, a2, pos, a3
        fuse bracket-turn, a3, neg, a2
    case a2
      fork case, read b
        fuse bracket-turn, a1, neg, a3
        fuse bracket-still, a2
        fuse bracket-turn, a3, pos, a1
    case a3
      fork case, read b
        fuse bracket-turn, a1, pos, a2
        fuse bracket-turn, a2, neg, a1
        fuse bracket-still, a3

# ALTERNATING: a generator brackets to zero with itself, [a,a] = 0. A rotation generates no turn against its own axis.
rule bracket-is-alternating
  seat a, like axis
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call bracket
        read a
        read a
      make still
  fold a

# ANTISYMMETRIC: [a,b] = -[b,a], the skew-symmetry that defines a Lie bracket. Swapping the order flips the sign. Over all
# nine generator pairs.
rule bracket-is-antisymmetric
  seat a, like axis
  seat b, like axis
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call bracket
        read a
        read b
      call flip-turn
        call bracket
          read b
          read a
  fold a, b
